### 1. Sign up (creates the account and returns a token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mike@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "fullName": "Mike Opima"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 2. Log in (returns a fresh token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mike@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### 3. Who am I? (protected - uses the token saved above)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Same call without a token -> 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### 5. Log in as the first admin (from application.properties)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@bookedly.local",
  "password": "admin-dev-password"
}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token); %}

### 6. Admin: list all users (find the id to promote)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Admin: promote user 2 to ADMIN (change the id to the one you want)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/users/2/promote
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8. Customer token on an admin endpoint -> 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Open days you can book (log in first with request 1 or 2)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/slots
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {% client.global.set("slotId", response.body[0].id); %}

### 10. Book the first open day from request 9 -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "slotId": {{slotId}}
}

### 11. Book the same day again -> 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "slotId": {{slotId}}
}
